		Puteri Suhaiza binti Sulaiman
		Shengguo Ge
		Shengjie Wang
		</p>
	<p>Point cloud registration remains challenging in complex environments due to noise, outliers, cluttered backgrounds, and incomplete observations. This paper proposes a segmentation-aided probabilistic framework for robust point cloud registration by integrating preprocessing, target-aware segmentation, and geometric-enhanced probabilistic registration into a unified pipeline. First, statistical outlier removal and density-based spatial clustering of applications with noise (DBSCAN) are employed to suppress noise and irrelevant points. Then, an improved particle swarm optimization (IPSO)-based segmentation method with morphological refinement is developed to extract target structures and reduce background interference. During registration, a covariance descriptor-enhanced coherent point drift (CPD) algorithm is introduced to improve local geometric representation and probabilistic correspondence estimation while maintaining structural consistency. Extensive experiments under noise disturbance, partial overlap conditions, and real-world point cloud scenarios demonstrate that the proposed framework achieves more accurate and stable registration performance compared with ICP, CPD, Improved CPD, and TEASER++. The results show that the proposed method reduces registration errors and improves convergence efficiency by combining structure-aware segmentation with geometric-enhanced probabilistic modeling. Unlike conventional methods that directly estimate correspondences from raw point clouds, the proposed framework reduces the influence of irrelevant points and unreliable correspondences through the cooperation of different processing stages. The proposed strategy provides an effective solution for robust point cloud registration in complex environments.</p>
	]]></content:encoded>

