        <item rdf:about="https://www.mdpi.com/2078-2489/17/10/946">

	<title>Information, Vol. 17, Pages 946: An Uncertainty-Aware Decision-Support System for Composite-Property Prediction with Physically Admissible Conformal Intervals</title>
	<link>https://www.mdpi.com/2078-2489/17/10/946</link>
	<description>Machine-learning surrogates predict composite properties but report no calibrated reliability and may violate physics. Bound-constrained conformal prediction confines intervals to physical bounds but assumes them exact. This paper keeps the corridor as a hard constraint and characterizes what a decision-support system guarantees when it is wrong. If a fraction &amp;amp;eta; of responses lies outside the corridor, no admissible interval covers more than 1&amp;amp;minus;&amp;amp;eta;, so the nominal level 1&amp;amp;minus;&amp;amp;alpha; is attainable only if &amp;amp;eta;&amp;amp;le;&amp;amp;alpha;. A projection-aware calibration scores out-of-corridor points as infinitely nonconforming. Its marginal coverage is at least 1&amp;amp;minus;&amp;amp;alpha;&amp;amp;minus;&amp;amp;eta;&amp;amp;pi;&amp;amp;infin; at every calibration size (&amp;amp;pi;&amp;amp;infin; the fallback probability); its coverage across calibrations follows an exact Beta law. In the limit it reaches the nominal level whenever attainable; calibrate-then-clip loses up to &amp;amp;eta;. For &amp;amp;eta;&amp;amp;lt;&amp;amp;alpha; the system thus delivers admissible intervals at the nominal level for a small, quantified width premium, with a feasibility verdict and a Shapley explanation. Across eight datasets it recovers the nominal level on a woven laminate with a misspecified rule-of-mixtures bound (90.3% against 85.6% for naive projection) and tracks the frontier under normative bounds the data contradict. Under exact Voigt&amp;amp;ndash;Reuss bounds it removes all violations and narrows intervals thirteen-fold. Width, paid inside the corridor, is the price.</description>
	<pubDate>2026-09-24</pubDate>

	<content:encoded><![CDATA[
	<p><b>Information, Vol. 17, Pages 946: An Uncertainty-Aware Decision-Support System for Composite-Property Prediction with Physically Admissible Conformal Intervals</b></p>
	<p>Information <a href="https://www.mdpi.com/2078-2489/17/10/946">doi: 10.3390/info17100946</a></p>
